  "estimatedMinutes": null,
  "statement": "Suppose \\(N\\) is a 6-digit number having base-10 representation \\(\\underline{a} \\underline{b} \\underline{c} \\underline{d} \\underline{e} \\underline{f}\\). If \\(N\\) is \\(6 / 7\\) of the number having base-10 representation \\(\\underline{d} \\underline{e} \\underline{f} \\underline{a} \\underline{b} \\underline{c}\\), find \\(N\\).",
  "answerChoices": [],
  "answer": {
    "letter": null,
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-general-1-2009-p2.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\(7(a b c d e f)_{10}=6(\\text { defabc })_{10}\\), so \\(699400 a+69940 b+6994 c=599300 d+59930 e+\\) \\(5993 f\\). We can factor this equation as \\(6994(100 a+10 b+c)=5993(100 d+10 e+f)\\), which yields \\(538(a b c)_{10}=461(d e f)_{10}\\). Since \\(\\operatorname{gcd}(538,461)=1\\), we must have \\((a b c)_{10}=461\\) and \\((d e f)_{10}=538\\).",
